patch -p1 << 'EOF'
From f16ea8a3b49c0e0f1e2177892baa7c65bdc6216f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Schauer Marin Rodrigues <josch@debian.org>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:32:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Debian Linux 7.2 and later ships vmlinuz in
 /usr/lib/modules/$ver/vmlinuz

"linux-version list" lists the kernels matching the glob
"/boot/vmlinu[xz]-*" but since Debian Linux 7.2, the location of vmlinuz
was moved from /boot into /usr/lib/modules/$ver. The binary package also
changed from linux-image-$ver to linux-binary-$ver in 6.19.

As a result, the function get_kernel_status would error out with kernel
7.2 because there is no longer any package shipping
"/boot/vmlinu[xz]-*". This commit works around this problem but there
are open questions:

 1. why does this function not just set pkg=linux-image-$ver or
    pkg=linux-binary-$ver
 2. is this function expected to return linux-image-$ver or, for kernels
    6.19 and later, linux-binary-$ver (this is the new behaviour now)
 3. is it sufficient to wait for the state being "installed" for
    linux-binary-$ver or should linux-image-$ver be "installed"?
 4. is it okay that the new version of this function disconnects the
    path to vmlinuz from the output of "linux-version list"? The path in
    /boot will not be populated at unpack time.
 5. is the use of "linux-version list" not wrong starting with kernel
    7.2 because linux-binary-$ver does no longer unpack the kernel to
    /boot?

Without this commit one gets the following error when running
flash-kernel:

dpkg-query: no packages found matching
run-parts: /etc/initramfs/post-update.d//flash-kernel exited with return code 1

Closes: #1148115
---
 functions | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/functions b/functions
index 7bb654b..fcc8469 100644
--- a/functions
+++ b/functions
@@ -601,8 +601,21 @@ get_kernel_status() {
 	# return the dpkg package status of kernel version $query_ver
 	local query_ver="$1"
 	local ver path pkg
+	#  version          | package with vmlinuz | location of vmlinuz
+	# ------------------+----------------------+----------------------------------
+	#  < 6.19           | linux-image-${ver}   | /boot/vmlinuz-${ver}
+	#  >= 6.19 && < 7.2 | linux-binary-${ver}  | /boot/vmlinuz-${ver}
+	#  >= 7.2           | linux-binary-${ver}  | /usr/lib/modules/${ver}/vmlinuz
 	linux-version list --paths | while read -r ver path; do
 		if linux-version compare "$ver" eq "$query_ver"; then
+			# since kernel 7.2, the image is shipped in
+			# /usr/lib/modules/$ver/vmlinuz
+			# the linux-version tool uses a glob on /boot/vmlinuz-*
+			if linux-version compare "$ver" ge "7.2"; then
+				path="/usr/lib/modules/$ver/vmlinuz"
+			fi
+			# FIXME: document why this function does not just set
+			# pkg=linux-image-$ver or pkg=linux-binary-$ver
 			pkg=$(
 				LANG=C.UTF-8 dpkg-query --search "$path" 2>/dev/null |
 				awk -F ": " -v path="$path" '$2==path { print $1; }'
-- 
2.55.0
EOF
